+
+Recorded calls accept a local absolute `drawing-completion.json` destination and a 64-character lowercase SHA-256 input identity. A native preflight refusal retains only `{version, input_sha256, outcome: "not_dispatched"}`; no engineering command was admitted. A successful call retains `{version, input_sha256, outcome: "completed", command_result, after}` with the exact atomic native observation. Downstream errors, missing or partial receipts prove neither completion nor refusal. Never repeat such an operation merely because its client stopped waiting. Retention is bounded to 256 KiB per receipt; failure preserves the reserved slot. Receipt reads do not require or mutate current document state. These bookkeeping identities are not authentication.
